  StartLine: Something in the reef remembers the old shapes.
  FeedingLine: 'It is feeding, rolled up round the plant - its guards circle it. Strike the body.'
  MealBrokenLine: Its meal is broken. It bolts.
  RisingLine: It has eaten enough. It rises into the Lord of the Dance.
  HaloLitLine: The halo is lit. Break the rings before the drum stops.
  FirstHaloLine: 'A ring is broken. Break {1} and the dance falls.'
  LastHaloLine: '{0} of {1}. One more ring!'
  CompletedLine: The Antlion has fed. The cycle is complete.
  WonLine: Its body is broken. The reef keeps its turn.
  DanceBrokenLine: The dance is broken. The reef keeps its turn.
  HeldOffLine: Time. You held it off - the cycle is unfinished.
  LungeLine: It turns on you - its guards are out round its jaws. Hurt it and it runs.
  SeveredLine: You cut it in two. The severed half crawls off to feed - stop it getting home.
  RejoinedLine: The severed half found its way home. It is whole again.
  SuccessionLine: 'You cut the body away - but the severed half lives, and it remembers the shape.'
  ChimeraLine: 'It is tearing between shapes - a whale, a jelly, neither. Strike it as it turns.'
  LearnedFeedingLine: 'It remembers being struck at the table. It eats far from you now, and bolts sooner.'
  LearnedLungingLine: It remembers what its lunges cost. It will not turn on you so readily.
  LearnedChasedLine: It remembers being run down. It feels you coming from farther away.
  LearnedSeveredLine: It remembers being cut in two. Its severed halves hurry home.
  RoamingLabel: Roaming
  WaryLabel: Wary
  FleeingLabel: Fleeing
  LungingLabel: Lunging - mind its guards
  FeedingLabel: Feeding - strike the body
  RisingLabel: Rising
  DancingLabel: Dancing - break the halo
